{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":23474670,"ns":0,"title":"Geometric progression","extract":"A geometric progression, also known as a geometric sequence, is a mathematical sequence of non-zero numbers where each term after the first is found by multiplying the previous one by a fixed number called the common ratio. For example, the sequence 2, 6, 18, 54, ...","description":"Mathematical sequence of numbers","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}